(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// memoryview's minimum (Objects/memoryobject.c), added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b): a view"] [10 1 "// of a bytes-like object's bytes, format 'B', one dimension: len, indexing and slicing, tobytes, tolist,"] [11 1 "// hex, release, the context manager, ==. _collections_abc registers the type at import. The buffer"] [12 1 "// protocol's other formats and shapes (cast, multi-dimensional views) are PY6's, with array and struct."] [16 1 "// MemoryView is a memoryview: its object, the start and length of its view, its step; released after"] [17 1 "// release()."] [22 24 "// \"\" is \"B\"; a cast's (PY6a): B b c H h I i L l Q q"] [23 2 "// PY7: exporter is the object a view of a class's __buffer__ (PEP 688) shows as obj (obj is then the view"] [24 2 "// __buffer__ returned); readonly a toreadonly's"] [27 2 "// mbuf is the export the view holds with the views made from it (queue 249, buffer_export.go): nil when its"] [28 2 "// exporter counts none"] [30 2 "// exports is the view's own (memory_getbuf's, and memory_hash's over the exporter's hash): release() refused while"] [31 2 "// any; hash once computed (queue 249)"] [35 2 "// shaped: the view is an exporter's PEP 3118 buffer (queue 260, BufferShaper: ctypes objects), its format, itemsize"] [36 2 "// isz and shape (ndim len(shape), 0 for a scalar) the exporter's, C-contiguous (start a byte offset, step 1)"] [42 1 "// BufferShaper is an exporter whose buffer is not a 1-D array of bytes (queue 260): Py_buffer's format, itemsize and"] [43 1 "// shape (ndim its length; strides NULL, so C-contiguous) as its getbufferproc gives them, ctypes' PyCData_NewGetBuffer."] [44 1 "// memoryview(o) of such an o is a view of that shape; its bytes are o's BytesLike, written through WritableBytes."] [49 1 "// shaperOf is o's BufferShaper (or its built-in value's), nil when o's buffer is plain bytes."] [60 1 "// viewOf is o's buffer described as a view (PyObject_GetBuffer): o itself when a memoryview, nil when no buffer."] [77 1 "// shapeList is view->shape."] [85 1 "// structFmt reports whether the struct module unpacks f (struct_get_unpacker): its byte orders, counts and codes only."] [95 1 "// ndim is view->ndim."] [103 1 "// nativeFmt is adjust_fmt's get_native_fmtstr for a shaped view: its format as a native single character ('@'"] [104 1 "// dropped), else NotImplementedError (ctypes' \"<i\", \"T{...}\": the struct module's, not memoryview's)."] [113 1 "// shapedList is tolist of a shaped view's dimension d at byte offset off (tolist_rec)."] [115 30 "// unpack_single: the format's own size"] [117 34 "// an item past a buffer of size 0 (an incomplete structure's \"B\"): CPython reads its zeroed b_value"] [133 1 "// shapedGet is memory_subscript of a shaped view."] [168 2 "// an index (memory_item), a tuple of indices (memory_item_multi), a tuple of slices, else invalid"] [229 1 "// derive registers nv, a view made from m (a slice, a cast, memoryview(m), toreadonly), with m's managed buffer."] [235 1 "// exportedObj is the view's obj attribute: the exporter's object."] [243 1 "// mvFlagsFullRO is PyBUF_FULL_RO, the flags memoryview() and bytes() ask a __buffer__ for."] [246 1 "// bufferOf is a class's __buffer__(flags): its memoryview, nil when the type has none (PY7: memoryview() and bytes()"] [247 1 "// of such an object raised TypeError)."] [263 1 "// releaseBuffer is PyBuffer_Release of a view bufferOf got: the exporter's __release_buffer__(view), when it has one."] [272 1 "// release is memoryview.release(): the exporter's buffer released once."] [306 1 "// item is the i-th item of a cast view: little-endian, signed for the lower-case formats."] [341 1 "// BytesLike makes a memoryview a bytes-like object (asBytes): a copy of its bytes."] [355 4 "// a view of a view: the same buffer, start, length and stride (CPython's memory_from_buffer keeps the"] [356 4 "// strides, so a non-contiguous view stays one)"] [363 42 "// picklebuf_getbuf: the object's own buffer"] [377 4 "// the export of a class's __buffer__: its __release_buffer__ called when the last view goes"] [386 40 "// queue 260: the exporter's format, itemsize and shape"] [392 2 "// memory_hash (queue 249): a read-only byte view's hash is its bytes' (hash(b'..')), the exporter hashed first with"] [393 2 "// the view exported meanwhile (gh-142664: a re-entrant __hash__ that releases the view gets BufferError)"] [474 2 "// item and slice assignment into a writable buffer (PY6d's REQUEST: _pyio's readinto, pickle's protocol 5"] [475 2 "// bytearray); byte views only"] [488 17 "// queue 260: a shaped view's items are the struct module's formats (memory_ass_sub's adjust_fmt)"] [562 3 "// queue 260 (memory_richcompare): views of other shapes differ (equiv_shape), and a format the struct module"] [563 3 "// cannot unpack (\"T{...}\", \"&<i\", \"<O\") makes the views unequal, a view itself included"] [598 17 "// queue 260: tolist_rec over the exporter's shape, native formats only (adjust_fmt)"] [632 32 "// queue 260: cast_to_1D's checks of a shaped source (memoryview_cast_impl's order)"] [651 4 "// a view of the same memory (writable through a bytearray's)"] [658 20 "// the same memory, so a writable view stays writable (PY6d's REQUEST)"] [671 2 "// count, index and toreadonly (PY7: absent): over tolist's items, as memory_count and memory_index"] [741 3 "// a 1-D view's shape, strides and contiguity (PY7: absent)"] [753 18 "// C-contiguous: init_strides_from_shape"] [779 34 "// CHECK_RELEASED (PY7: obj stayed readable; no attribute \"released\", CPython's has none)"] [787 1 "// unusable is the view's CHECK_RELEASED, and its exporter's own check when it has one (queue 204: an mmap closed under"] [788 1 "// the view raises ValueError \"mmap closed or invalid\", where CPython's mmap refuses the close; pyi counts no exports)."] [799 1 "// isReadonly is view->readonly: a toreadonly's or __buffer__'s view, or one of an exporter that is not writable (queue 249:"] [800 1 "// an array's buffer is writable, as arraymodule.c exports it; only a bytearray's was before)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[51 30] [54 44] [62 29] [70 22] [107 28] [136 25] [152 25] [171 24] [174 28] [177 26] [189 33] [249 47] [265 55] [285 17] [287 16] [310 17] [310 25] [328 24] [333 24] [333 33] [354 33] [363 35] [364 24] [369 37] [386 26] [399 25] [405 19] [408 26] [435 25] [448 25] [454 26] [478 25] [490 27] [494 30] [511 26] [524 14] [524 21] [564 42] [580 40] [680 42] [700 42] [711 14] [711 37] [756 30] [756 38] [793 68]] :go/trails [[775 5]]} (go/file "memoryview.go" :imports [


